<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH DANONE-NESTLE UNIT TO PAY CZK 70 GROSS DIV.</title>
<headline>CZECH DANONE-NESTLE UNIT TO PAY CZK 70 GROSS DIV.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Czech confectioner Cokoladovny a.s. , majority owned by a consortium comprised of Groupe Danone and Nestle SA voted on Monday to pay out a 70 crown gross dividend per share on 1996 earnings after 50 crowns previous year, the Czech news agency CTK reported.</p>
